==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|milk|y}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪɫki/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪlki}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|milk|ier}}

# Resembling [[milk]] in [[color]]/[[colour]] or [[consistency]].
# (''colour science, informal'') Of the [[black]] in an [[image]], appearing as dark [[grey]]/[[gray]] rather than black.
# {{colloquial}} Cowardly. Possibly coined by Graham Greene in the novel ''Brighton Rock'' (1938).

